      "value": "@{64873f159cf028090ce2c2e2|full_name}\n\nWith respect, the concern here isn't whether VRChat crashes other programs intentionally — no one in the thread is arguing that. The issue is that VRChat's documentation, system requirements, and known-issues pages do not disclose that running it alongside certain applications (League of Legends with Vanguard being the most frequently cited example) can cause those applications to crash.\n\nThere's also a practical problem with redirecting users to Riot support: Riot is very likely to respond the same way in reverse — 'this appears to be caused by a third-party application, please contact them.' Neither side acknowledging the interaction leaves affected users with no actual path to a resolution.\n\n'Not intentional' and 'not disclosed' are two different claims, and only one of them is being made here. A brief entry on the known issues page would let users make an informed decision before the crash happens, not after.",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
    }
