  "details": "I'm experiencing frequent, sudden crashes of the League of Legends client during gameplay — specifically in both Summoner’s Rift and ARAM matches. After extensive testing, I have reason to believe VRChat may be contributing to or causing this issue due to a software conflict.\n\nHere's what I have observed and tried:\n\nThe crashes occur even after a clean reinstall of Windows\n\nNVIDIA GPU drivers and Windows Updates are fully up-to-date\n\nI’ve run the Hextech Repair Tool and followed all official League crash troubleshooting steps\n\nDespite all of the above, the crashes persisted\n\nHowever, when I closed VRChat and OBS, then launched only League of Legends, no crashes occurred during the same type of gameplay session (ARAM). This strongly suggests that running VRChat concurrently with League may be contributing to or triggering the crash.\n\nI am submitting this report in case VRChat is interfering with other full-screen or GPU-intensive applications in a way that could lead to instability or client crashes.",
